;; A, the Throat. You fall from the heart (bowl (12,9)) down column 12 onto
;; the landing floor (row 5). Column 12 is a steady lift (^) from the
;; landing up through the seam, the heart's cell and the bowl's (12,8)
;; (the bowl room's air-field); the rough pillar at column 13 is the climb
;; back without the down, continuing as % at bowl (13,9..10). West, the
;; shaft (columns 3-5) drops to E, its east wall rough (column 6) for the
;; climb back. East, the landing runs on into B (rows 4-5). Across the
;; shaft to the west, a false wall (2, rows 4-5) hides the first carving.
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (4 4)
  title: "The Throat"
  intent: "under the heart a throat of dark stone falls away, and the hum you woke to is all around you"
  bed: (hum 0.8 air 0.4 water 0 drone 0.6)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("############^%###########"
   "############^%###########"
   "####### #   ^%  ## ######"
   "###         ^%      ## ##"
   "# +         ^%           "
   "# +         ^            "
   "###   %##################"
   "###   %##################"
   "###   %##################"
   "###   %##################"
   "###   %##################")
  decor: none)
